-- Decision Ledger — Seed Data
-- Tells a 6-month story (Jan–Jun 2026) for Nexura Commerce,
-- a US-based subscription wellness & beauty box expanding into Europe.
-- Status mix across reviewed decisions: ~70% succeeded, 15% failed, 11% reversed, 4% superseded.

BEGIN;

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- PRICING (10 decisions)
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

INSERT INTO decisions (id, title, category, context, options_considered, data_consulted,
  decision_made, rationale, expected_outcome, review_date, status, actual_outcome, team, owner, decided_at)
VALUES
(1,
 'Raise base subscription price from $45 to $49 per month',
 'pricing',
 'Nexura has held its base price for 22 months. COGS rose 11% in 2025 driven by ingredient costs and carrier rate increases. Gross margin has compressed from 58% to 51% over that period. The competitive median price is $52/month. NPS sits at 68 — a company record — suggesting meaningful pricing power exists.',
 '[{"option":"Hold at $45","pros":["zero churn risk","no customer communication required"],"cons":["margin continues to compress","signals brand weakness"]},{"option":"Raise to $49","pros":["$48/subscriber/year uplift","still $3 below competitor median","funds roadmap investment"],"cons":["estimated 2-4% churn among price-sensitive cohort"]},{"option":"Raise to $52 matching competitors","pros":["maximum margin recovery"],"cons":["high churn risk","sacrifices primary positioning advantage"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Competitor pricing survey Jan 2026','Price elasticity cohort model (n=12,400)','NPS survey Q4 2025','COGS breakdown report Dec 2025','Churn cohort analysis by tenure'],
 'Raise base monthly price from $45 to $49, effective 1 Feb 2026, with 60-day advance notice. Offer existing subscribers a 3-month price-lock if they prepay before the change date.',
 'At $49 we remain below the $52 competitor median while recovering approximately $1.8M in ARR. Cohort data shows churn under 3% for price increases below $5. The prepay price-lock converts potential churners into cash-paid retention.',
 'Churn rate ≤3% at 90-day review; net ARR lift ≥$1.5M; subscriber NPS does not fall below 62.',
 '2026-06-05',
 'succeeded',
 'Churn rate at 90-day mark: 2.1% — within threshold. ARR increased $2.4M (8.9% lift). Net subscriber count grew 340, 4.2% above forecast. Price-lock offer used by 9% of subscribers, effectively absorbing the highest-churn-risk cohort.',
 'Finance',
 'Nadia Osei',
 '2026-01-05 09:00:00+00'),

(2,
 'Introduce 20% discount for annual billing commitment',
 'pricing',
 'Monthly churn averages 3.8%. Industry data shows annual-plan subscribers churn at 0.6–1.2% annually. We currently have no annual billing option. Offering 20% off annual (effective $43.20/month) is margin-accretive versus a churned monthly subscriber because retention saves the $28 CAC replacement cost.',
 '[{"option":"No change — keep monthly only","pros":["simplicity"],"cons":["miss retention lever","above-average churn persists"]},{"option":"20% annual discount ($432/year)","pros":["locks in 12 months of revenue","churn near 0% for annual cohort","upfront cash improves working capital"],"cons":["20% revenue cut on converted subscribers"]},{"option":"15% annual discount","pros":["smaller revenue haircut"],"cons":["less compelling — industry data shows 20% is the conversion threshold"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['SaaS annual plan conversion benchmarks (Recurly 2025)','Internal cohort churn data 2024-2025','LTV model: monthly vs annual subscriber','Working capital forecast Q1 2026'],
 'Launch annual billing at $432/year (20% discount vs monthly). Promote to subscribers with 6+ months tenure via in-app banner and email campaign.',
 'The NPV of a retained annual subscriber ($432 guaranteed) exceeds the NPV of a monthly subscriber who has a 3.8% monthly churn risk. At 6+ months tenure we know they have demonstrated value; the offer converts loyalty into commitment.',
 'Annual plan attach rate ≥20% within 90 days of launch; upfront cash collected ≥$800K; annual-plan 12-month retention ≥92%.',
 '2026-04-12',
 'succeeded',
 'Annual plan attach rate reached 28% within 90 days, exceeding the 20% target. Upfront cash of $1.24M collected in the first billing cycle. 12-month retention tracking at 94% on early cohort (60-day proxy via cancel-intent surveys).',
 'Finance',
 'Nadia Osei',
 '2026-01-12 10:00:00+00'),

(3,
 'Launch $29/month Essentials tier with reduced box size',
 'pricing',
 'Funnel data shows a 34% drop-off at the payment step for new visitors. Exit surveys cite price as the top barrier. Hypothesis: a $29 entry tier captures price-sensitive prospects who would otherwise not convert, without cannibalizing the core $49 tier.',
 '[{"option":"No entry tier — hold single SKU","pros":["simple pricing","avoids cannibalization"],"cons":["high price-barrier drop-off continues"]},{"option":"$29 Essentials (4 items vs 7 in core)","pros":["removes price barrier","creates upgrade path"],"cons":["cannibalization risk if existing subscribers downgrade","thinner margin on smaller box"]},{"option":"Free trial (first box $10)","pros":["lowest barrier","proven acquisition tactic"],"cons":["expensive subsidy","high post-trial churn historically"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Checkout funnel analysis Dec 2025','Exit survey data (n=2,200)','Tiered-pricing impact study (McKinsey 2024)','COGS model for reduced-size box','Competitor tier analysis'],
 'Launch $29 Essentials tier (4-item box) in February. Run for 90 days and evaluate cannibalization vs. incremental subscriber impact.',
 'Exit survey data strongly suggests price is the conversion barrier. A reduced-size, lower-cost tier can serve price-sensitive segments without product change. If cannibalization exceeds 8% of core subscribers, we will sunset the tier.',
 'Net new incremental subscribers +500 in 90 days with cannibalization of existing $49 subscribers ≤8%; overall ARR neutral or positive.',
 '2026-05-03',
 'failed',
 'Essentials tier launched Feb 15. Within 45 days, 18% of existing $49 subscribers downgraded — 3× the 6% risk threshold. Net ARR declined $210K. Incremental new subscribers: 180, far short of the 500 target. Tier discontinued April 1. Key learning: value segmentation is inadequate for physical goods where fulfillment cost difference is small.',
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-02-03 11:00:00+00'),

(4,
 'Deploy dynamic pricing algorithm for new subscriber acquisition',
 'pricing',
 'CAC is rising ($41 in Q4 2025 vs $33 in Q4 2024). Paid acquisition channels are showing diminishing returns at fixed price. Proposal: use ML-driven dynamic pricing on acquisition landing pages, offering $39–$49 depending on traffic source, time of day, and propensity-to-convert score.',
 '[{"option":"Fixed $49 price for all acquisition","pros":["simple","no fairness perception risk"],"cons":["CAC continues rising","lost conversions at margin"]},{"option":"Dynamic pricing $39–$49 on acquisition pages","pros":["optimize conversion rate","potential CAC reduction 15-20%"],"cons":["customer fairness risk","brand inconsistency","technical complexity"]},{"option":"Promotional codes via partners only","pros":["targeted discounts","less visible than dynamic pricing"],"cons":["limited scale","partner dependency"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['CAC trend analysis 2024-2025','Conversion rate optimization audit','Dynamic pricing case studies (Uber, airlines)','Legal review: price discrimination risk memo'],
 'Deploy dynamic pricing to 15% of new acquisition traffic as an A/B test. Monitor conversion rate, CAC, and customer complaint signals for 30 days.',
 'Personalized pricing is standard in travel and hospitality. Small variation in acquisition pricing (within $10) should be invisible to most customers since pricing is session-specific and not publicly indexed.',
 'CAC reduction ≥15% in dynamic pricing cohort; conversion rate improvement ≥10%; customer complaint volume does not increase materially.',
 '2026-03-18',
 'reversed',
 'Dynamic pricing deployed to 15% traffic on Feb 20. Within 6 hours, subscribers began sharing screenshots on Reddit and Twitter showing price differences. Complaint volume spiked 280% intraday. Decision reversed and algorithm disabled after 22 hours. A public blog post apologizing for the "test" was required. Key lesson: physical subscription products carry different fairness expectations than digital or travel services.',
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-02-18 14:00:00+00'),

(5,
 'Raise gift subscription price by 10% across all tiers',
 'pricing',
 'Gift subscriptions represent 22% of Q4 revenue and have been priced at a 5% discount to regular subscriptions since 2023. Post-holiday analysis shows gifters are highly price-insensitive (NPS among gifters: 74). COGS for gift boxes is 8% higher due to premium packaging. Aligning gift pricing to a slight premium captures real cost structure.',
 '[{"option":"Hold gift pricing","pros":["no risk to gifting volume"],"cons":["continuing margin gap on gift COGS"]},{"option":"Raise gift price 10%","pros":["aligns with real COGS","gifters are price-insensitive","holiday gifting is occasion-driven not price-driven"],"cons":["small risk of gifting volume drop"]},{"option":"Remove gift discount entirely (15% raise)","pros":["full margin recovery"],"cons":["meaningful price shock on premium gift SKUs"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Gift subscription margin analysis Q4 2025','Gifter NPS survey (n=890)','Price sensitivity regression: gift vs. self-purchase cohorts','Competitor gift pricing analysis'],
 'Raise all gift subscription prices by 10%, effective March 15. Update all gift landing pages. Run at full price through Q2.',
 'Gifter cohort shows NPS 74 vs 68 for regular subscribers — they are our most satisfied and least price-sensitive buyers. A 10% increase on occasion-driven gifts is unlikely to change decision to purchase since the primary variable is occasion relevance, not price.',
 'Gift subscription revenue +8% vs prior 90-day period; gift unit volume decline ≤5%.',
 '2026-06-10',
 'succeeded',
 'Gift revenue increased 19% vs prior 90 days. Gift unit volume declined 1.8% — well within the 5% threshold. Average order value on multi-month gift bundles increased $14.20.',
 'Finance',
 'Nadia Osei',
 '2026-03-10 09:30:00+00'),

(6,
 'Launch loyalty pricing: 15% discount for subscribers 12+ months',
 'pricing',
 'Long-tenure subscribers (12mo+) have a 91% annual retention rate and NPS of 79 but generate the same margin as new subscribers. Competitors have started introducing loyalty tiers. Risk: if we do not reward loyalty, high-NPS long-tenure subscribers could be poached when competitors target them with discounts.',
 '[{"option":"No loyalty pricing","pros":["protects margin"],"cons":["vulnerability to competitor poaching","missed retention signal opportunity"]},{"option":"15% discount at 12mo anniversary","pros":["rewards highest-LTV segment","signals commitment to long-term relationship","low cost: already 91% retained"],"cons":["margin reduction on customers who would have stayed anyway"]},{"option":"Free gift at anniversary instead of discount","pros":["tangible reward","no MRR reduction"],"cons":["operationally complex","less compelling than cash savings"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Subscriber tenure retention curve analysis','Competitor loyalty program benchmarking','LTV model: tenure cohorts','Churn hazard model by tenure bucket'],
 'Introduce 15% loyalty discount for subscribers reaching their 12-month anniversary, applied automatically at renewal.',
 'At 12 months the subscriber has already demonstrated strong LTV signals. The 15% discount costs ~$88/year but retains a subscriber worth ~$520 annual ARR with 91% baseline retention. The marginal cost of the discount is well below the CAC of a replacement subscriber ($41).',
 'Loyalty-discount cohort 12-month retention ≥95%; no material cannibalization of shorter-tenure upgrade path.',
 '2026-07-25',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Finance',
 'Nadia Osei',
 '2026-03-25 10:00:00+00'),

(7,
 'Launch $69/month bundle combining Skincare and Wellness boxes',
 'pricing',
 'We operate two separate box lines: Skincare ($49) and Wellness ($49). Cross-category analysis shows 14% of customers subscribe to both (paying $98). A $69 bundle captures customers interested in both lines at lower cost while upselling single-category subscribers. Bundling is a proven retention mechanic.',
 '[{"option":"Keep separate boxes at $49 each","pros":["simple existing model"],"cons":["no upsell lever","$98 dual-box price is high"]},{"option":"$69 combined bundle","pros":["$20 savings vs dual-box","strong upsell narrative","increases units per subscriber"],"cons":["bundle discount reduces ARR for existing dual-box subscribers","requires supply chain coordination"]},{"option":"$79 bundle (smaller discount)","pros":["less ARR dilution"],"cons":["less compelling vs $29 savings"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Dual-subscriber cohort analysis','Category cross-sell propensity model','Bundle pricing case studies','Supply chain capacity check with fulfillment partner'],
 'Launch $69/month Nexura Complete bundle combining 5 Skincare + 4 Wellness items in a single box. Target single-category subscribers via upgrade campaign.',
 'Bundle pricing reduces the effective per-unit cost for the consumer while increasing our revenue per customer vs single-box. The $69 price creates a natural upgrade path from either $49 product and improves box utilization economics.',
 'Bundle conversion: ≥8% of single-category subscribers upgrade within 90 days; dual-box subscriber migration ≥60% adopt bundle (at $69 vs $98); overall bundle ARR contribution +$400K.',
 '2026-08-08',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-04-08 11:00:00+00'),

(8,
 'Set UK market pricing in GBP with local purchasing power parity',
 'pricing',
 'Nexura UK launched in January (see decision 33). We are currently billing UK customers in USD at the $49 equivalent, creating FX exposure and a poor customer experience. Local GBP pricing at £38/month (vs direct conversion £39.50) aligns with UK subscription market norms and removes FX friction.',
 '[{"option":"Keep billing in USD","pros":["simple, no FX ops changes"],"cons":["customer friction","FX exposure on revenue","UK market norms expect local currency"]},{"option":"£38/month GBP pricing","pros":["market-norm pricing","removes FX risk","improves conversion on UK-origin traffic"],"cons":["GBP/USD fluctuation creates ARR reporting complexity"]},{"option":"£40/month (full conversion)","pros":["maximizes revenue at current rates"],"cons":["above-market vs UK competitors avg £37"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['UK subscription market pricing report (Statista 2025)','FX exposure analysis Q1 2026','UK competitor pricing survey','Stripe UK billing capabilities review'],
 'Switch UK billing to £38/month GBP. Update all UK-facing pages, emails, and Stripe configuration by May 15.',
 'Customers in the UK expect local currency billing. Local GBP pricing is standard practice for all serious UK market entrants. The slight discount vs direct conversion (£0.50/month) is negligible against the conversion improvement and FX risk elimination.',
 'UK checkout conversion rate +15%; FX-related support tickets reduced to zero; UK MRR reported cleanly in GBP.',
 '2026-08-02',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Finance',
 'Nadia Osei',
 '2026-05-02 09:00:00+00'),

(9,
 'Establish flash sale cadence: quarterly 72-hour 30% off promotions',
 'pricing',
 'We have run ad-hoc promotions with inconsistent results. Analysis of past promotions shows they generate 2–4× normal acquisition volume during the window but the incremental LTV of promotion-acquired subscribers is 22% lower. A structured quarterly cadence creates predictability for planning while limiting discount exposure to 4 days per year.',
 '[{"option":"No flash sales — full-price only","pros":["protects brand and margin","predictable revenue"],"cons":["missed acquisition peaks","competitor promotions go unchallenged"]},{"option":"Quarterly 72-hour 30% off promotions","pros":["creates urgency","predictable acquisition bursts","manageable 4 days per year discount exposure"],"cons":["promotion-acquired LTV 22% lower","potential training customers to wait for sales"]},{"option":"Monthly 20% off first box","pros":["more consistent offer"],"cons":["always-on discounting trains price sensitivity"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Historical promotion performance analysis 2024-2025','LTV cohort: promotion vs. organic acquisition','Competitor promotional calendar mapping','Gross margin impact model: quarterly flash sale scenario'],
 'Run quarterly 72-hour flash sales at 30% off first month. Schedule: Q3 (Aug), Q4 (Nov — Black Friday adjacent), Q1 2027 (Feb — post-holiday), Q2 2027 (May).',
 'A structured cadence is more defensible than ad-hoc promotions because it enables supply chain planning, content preparation, and marketing budget pre-allocation. 4 days of discounting per year is manageable against the acquisition upside.',
 'Each flash sale window: ≥600 new subscriber acquisitions; blended quarterly CAC does not exceed $48; promotion subscriber 90-day retention ≥70%.',
 '2026-08-20',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-05-20 14:00:00+00'),

(10,
 'Implement channel price parity policy across all distribution points',
 'pricing',
 'Nexura products are sold via our website, iOS app, and two retail partner pop-ups. App store billing adds a 30% Apple commission, retail partners take 25% margin, while our direct channel has zero distribution cost. Currently prices are inconsistent — retail is 15% higher, app has no adjustment. This creates customer confusion and arbitrage.',
 '[{"option":"No change — allow price variance by channel","pros":["simple, no price adjustments"],"cons":["customer confusion","arbitrage between channels","difficult to enforce MAP"]},{"option":"Enforce price parity everywhere","pros":["clean customer experience","simplified marketing","no arbitrage"],"cons":["app and retail economics become worse; may need to exit retail partnerships"]},{"option":"Direct channel optimization: close retail, keep app (raise app price to cover Apple fee)","pros":["maximizes direct margin","cleaner economics"],"cons":["lose retail brand presence","app price increase risks rating impact"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Channel margin analysis by distribution point','Apple App Store commission policy review','Retail partner contract terms audit','Customer channel-switching survey'],
 'Enforce price parity: all channels sell at $49. Renegotiate retail partnership terms to a flat referral fee model. Investigate Apple Small Business Program to reduce app commission.',
 'Price parity is a prerequisite for brand consistency and prevents customers from arbitraging channels. The App Store and retail economics need to be renegotiated separately rather than baking the cost into consumer pricing.',
 'Zero customer complaints about price discrepancy across channels; retail partner contract renegotiation completed Q3 2026.',
 '2026-09-03',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Finance',
 'Nadia Osei',
 '2026-06-03 10:00:00+00');


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- PRODUCT (12 decisions)
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

INSERT INTO decisions (id, title, category, context, options_considered, data_consulted,
  decision_made, rationale, expected_outcome, review_date, status, actual_outcome, team, owner, decided_at)
VALUES
(11,
 'Launch Nexura iOS mobile application',
 'product',
 'Mobile accounts for 61% of website traffic but only 31% of conversions. The gap between mobile traffic and conversion is the single largest revenue leak in our funnel. A native app addresses this via saved payment methods, push notifications, and faster load times. iOS first because 68% of mobile visitors use iPhone.',
 '[{"option":"Continue mobile web only","pros":["no development cost","one codebase"],"cons":["persistent 30-point conversion gap vs desktop","no push notification capability","no App Store presence"]},{"option":"iOS app first, Android 90 days later","pros":["ships faster","captures 68% of mobile visitors","App Store presence signals legitimacy"],"cons":["Android users wait 90 days"]},{"option":"React Native cross-platform simultaneously","pros":["one codebase for both platforms","simultaneous launch"],"cons":["slower initial development","cross-platform UX quality often lower"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Mobile traffic vs conversion funnel analysis Dec 2025','iOS vs Android split on Nexura mobile traffic (Google Analytics)','App store optimization competitive analysis','React Native vs native build cost estimate'],
 'Build and ship native iOS app. Target App Store submission by end of January, public launch by February 1. Android development begins in parallel targeting April launch.',
 'A native app will close the mobile conversion gap via frictionless checkout (Apple Pay), push notification re-engagement, and superior performance. iOS first because 68% of mobile visitors are on iPhone and we can move fastest with a single platform to start.',
 'App Store rating ≥4.5/5 within 60 days; ≥50% of active subscribers adopt app as primary channel within 90 days; push notification opt-in rate ≥40%.',
 '2026-04-08',
 'succeeded',
 'App Store rating: 4.7/5 from 11,400 reviews at 90-day mark. 68% of active subscribers now use the app as primary channel. Push notification opt-in rate: 38% (slightly below 40% target but above industry median of 31%). Mobile conversion rate improved from 31% to 54%.',
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-01-08 09:00:00+00'),

(12,
 'Redesign personalization quiz with adaptive branching logic (v2)',
 'product',
 'The current 8-question linear quiz has a 61% completion rate. Post-quiz product relevance ratings average 3.1/5. Qualitative research shows customers find questions generic. V2 hypothesis: adaptive branching (skip irrelevant questions based on prior answers) improves completion and relevance.',
 '[{"option":"Keep v1 quiz unchanged","pros":["stable baseline","no development cost"],"cons":["61% completion is a known revenue leak","low product relevance dissatisfies subscribers"]},{"option":"Adaptive v2 quiz (5–12 questions depending on path)","pros":["higher completion","better personalization data","improved first-box relevance"],"cons":["2-week dev effort","risk of over-engineering"]},{"option":"Skip quiz — use purchase history and browsing to personalize","pros":["no friction for new users"],"cons":["no data for first box — cold start problem"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Quiz funnel analysis: drop-off by question (Mixpanel)','Post-box survey: product relevance rating 2025','Qualitative user interviews (n=18) Dec 2025','A/B test framework capacity check'],
 'Build adaptive-branching quiz v2. Minimum 5 questions, maximum 12, with branching based on skin type, lifestyle, and goal inputs. Run as A/B test for 30 days, full rollout if conversion and relevance improve.',
 'The primary failure mode of v1 is generic questions that do not adapt to the respondent, resulting in low relevance scores. Adaptive branching solves this without adding friction — customers only see questions relevant to their path.',
 'Quiz completion rate ≥80% (vs 61% baseline); post-box relevance rating ≥4.0/5; 90-day subscriber retention for v2 completers ≥85%.',
 '2026-04-15',
 'succeeded',
 'Quiz completion rate: 84% (vs 61% baseline — +23 points). Post-box relevance rating: 4.2/5. 90-day retention for v2 quiz completers: 87% vs 74% for non-completers. A/B test showed clear winner at day 18; rolled out fully on Feb 25.',
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-01-15 11:00:00+00'),

(13,
 'Build AI-powered product recommendation engine for the subscriber dashboard',
 'product',
 'Subscribers currently see a static "You might also like" section with no personalization. Add-on purchase rate is 8.4%. With Priya Menon (Head of Data Science) onboarded in February, we now have the ML capability to build a collaborative filtering recommendation engine trained on purchase and engagement history.',
 '[{"option":"Keep static recommendations","pros":["no engineering cost"],"cons":["8.4% add-on rate is low","missed revenue per subscriber"]},{"option":"Collaborative filtering recommendation engine","pros":["personalized at scale","proven lift in e-commerce (Netflix, Amazon)","feeds data flywheel"],"cons":["requires 6–8 weeks of engineering time","cold-start problem for new subscribers"]},{"option":"Rule-based personalization (if skin type=dry, show X)","pros":["fast to build","interpretable"],"cons":["does not learn over time","limited to static rules"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Add-on purchase funnel analysis','Recommendation engine benchmark study (McKinsey e-commerce report 2025)','Data Science team capacity plan Q1 2026','Subscriber engagement and purchase history dataset (18 months)'],
 'Build collaborative filtering recommendation engine using subscriber purchase history, quiz answers, and box engagement signals. Deploy to subscriber dashboard and post-ship email.',
 'We now have 18 months of purchase data and a dedicated data science team. Collaborative filtering is the proven approach for personalized product discovery. The cold-start problem is mitigated by falling back to quiz-based recommendations for subscribers with <3 purchases.',
 'Add-on purchase rate lifts from 8.4% to ≥12%; recommendation click-through rate ≥20%; user-rated relevance ≥4.0/5 in post-click survey.',
 '2026-05-05',
 'succeeded',
 'Add-on purchase rate: 13.1% (vs 8.4% baseline — +4.7pp). Recommendation CTR: 26%. Relevance rating: 4.3/5. Incremental add-on revenue in first 90 days: $420K. Cold-start fallback (quiz-based) performed within 8% of the personalized engine for new subscribers.',
 'Product',
 'Priya Menon',
 '2026-02-05 10:00:00+00'),

(14,
 'Launch virtual try-on AR feature for skincare product selection',
 'product',
 'Beauty industry reports show AR try-on features drive 30–40% conversion lifts (ModiFace, Perfect Corp data). We hypothesize that allowing subscribers to preview how foundation and lip colors look on their face before box curation will increase satisfaction and reduce returns. The technology is licensable from Perfect Corp at $8K/month.',
 '[{"option":"No AR feature","pros":["$96K/year cost avoided"],"cons":["miss potential conversion lift","competitors deploying AR (Sephora, Ulta)"]},{"option":"License Perfect Corp AR SDK for 90-day trial","pros":["fastest path","proven technology","no in-house ML required"],"cons":["$24K for 90-day trial","dependency on third-party vendor","may not suit our non-makeup box positioning"]},{"option":"Build in-house AR using Apple ARKit","pros":["full ownership","customizable"],"cons":["6+ month build","high engineering cost"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['ModiFace AR conversion lift report 2025','Perfect Corp SDK demo and pricing','Internal: product category split (skincare vs makeup) in subscriber boxes','User research: interest in AR try-on (survey n=1,400)'],
 'License Perfect Corp AR SDK for a 90-day paid trial. Integrate into the product selection screen for the 40% of boxes that include color cosmetics. Measure engagement and conversion against control group.',
 'Industry data shows meaningful lift for color cosmetics. Our subscriber base includes color cosmetics in 40% of boxes, giving us a reasonable target population. The 90-day trial limits our exposure to $24K while validating the hypothesis.',
 'AR feature engagement rate ≥20% of eligible subscribers; box satisfaction score for AR users ≥4.3/5; trial ROI positive (incremental revenue ≥$24K in 90 days).',
 '2026-05-20',
 'failed',
 'AR feature engagement rate: 4.2% — 5× below the 20% target. Exit survey with non-users (n=890): 72% rated the feature "too inaccurate to be useful" for skincare shading. Satisfaction scores showed no difference between AR and non-AR groups. Cost: $24K trial fee + $60K engineering integration. Feature deprecated after 60 days. Key learning: AR try-on is validated for makeup but our skincare-heavy positioning does not benefit. Research before licensing next time.',
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-02-20 14:00:00+00'),

(15,
 'Transition to 100% recycled and biodegradable outer packaging',
 'product',
 'Subscriber survey shows 81% consider environmental impact when choosing subscription boxes. Our current packaging uses virgin cardboard and plastic void fill. Switching to recycled cardboard + biodegradable kraft paper fill has been quoted by our supplier at the same price as current packaging via a volume-commitment deal.',
 '[{"option":"Keep current packaging","pros":["no change","established supply chain"],"cons":["reputational lag vs sustainability-focused competitors","81% of subscribers say it matters to them"]},{"option":"100% recycled/biodegradable packaging at same cost via volume commit","pros":["brand alignment","no cost increase","strong PR and NPS opportunity"],"cons":["supply chain change risk","volume commit is 18 months"]},{"option":"Partial transition (outer box only)","pros":["lower volume commitment"],"cons":["half-measure dilutes marketing message"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Subscriber sustainability survey Jan 2026 (n=3,200)','Supplier quote: EcoPackaging Partners Feb 2026','Brand sentiment analysis: sustainability mentions (Brandwatch)','Competitor packaging audit'],
 'Commit to full transition to recycled outer box + biodegradable kraft fill by March 31. Sign 18-month volume commitment with EcoPackaging Partners.',
 'Cost-neutral sustainability is a clear win. 81% of subscribers cite environmental impact as important, and the volume-commit deal makes this cost-neutral. The 18-month commitment is manageable given current subscriber count stability.',
 'NPS improvement ≥5 points within 90 days of rebrand announcement; zero damage-rate increase vs current packaging; no COGS increase.',
 '2026-06-03',
 'succeeded',
 'NPS improved 8 points (68→76) in first post-transition survey — above the 5-point target. Damage rate: 2.1% vs 2.0% baseline — statistically equivalent. COGS: zero increase (volume commitment honored). Social media positive mentions of "eco packaging" up 34%. Supplier delivery reliability: 98% on time.',
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-03-03 09:00:00+00'),

(16,
 'Add subscription pause feature: up to 2 months per year',
 'product',
 'Exit survey data shows 31% of cancellations cite "taking a break" or "travelling" rather than product dissatisfaction. These are structurally recoverable — subscribers who want to pause but cannot are forced to cancel. A pause feature retains the subscriber relationship through a temporary life event.',
 '[{"option":"No pause feature — cancel or continue","pros":["simpler billing logic"],"cons":["31% of cancels are structurally preventable","forces cancel for temporary situations"]},{"option":"Pause up to 2 months/year","pros":["captures 31% recoverable cancels","maintains relationship","industry standard (Birchbox, FabFitFun have this)"],"cons":["small MRR dip while paused","engineering complexity in billing system"]},{"option":"Skip a box (single month)","pros":["simpler implementation"],"cons":["does not address multi-month travel/life events"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Exit survey: cancellation reason analysis 2025','Competitor feature audit: pause availability','Stripe billing pause API capability review','Estimated pause utilization model'],
 'Build and launch subscription pause feature: subscribers can pause for 1 or 2 months, up to twice per year. Paused subscribers retain access to subscriber-only content and early access deals.',
 'If 31% of cancels are pause-motivated and we retain even 40% of those with a pause option, that is ~120 subscribers per month saved at $49 each = $70K ARR annually at current scale. Engineering cost is one sprint.',
 'Pause feature usage by ≥10% of cancel-intent subscribers; 90-day return rate for paused subscribers ≥60%; net cancellation rate decrease ≥0.5pp.',
 '2026-06-18',
 'succeeded',
 'Pause feature used by 14% of subscribers who initiated a cancel flow — above the 10% target. Of paused subscribers, 71% reactivated after their pause period. Net cancellation rate fell 0.8pp (from 3.8% to 3.0%). Estimated ARR saved in first 90 days: $88K.',
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-03-18 11:00:00+00'),

(17,
 'Launch Nexura Android mobile application',
 'product',
 'The iOS app launched February 1 and exceeded all targets. Android represents 32% of mobile visitors who still have no native app option. With iOS app architecture finalized, Android development can leverage shared React Native components for the checkout flow, reducing build time.',
 '[{"option":"Delay Android — iOS focus only","pros":["avoid fragmentation","iOS subscribers generate higher LTV"],"cons":["32% of mobile visitors underserved","Android share growing in EU target markets"]},{"option":"Native Android app","pros":["best Android experience","full platform access"],"cons":["longer build time — estimated 14 weeks"]},{"option":"React Native port of iOS app","pros":["faster — estimated 8 weeks","shared codebase reduces maintenance"],"cons":["slightly lower performance than native on some Android versions"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Android vs iOS traffic and LTV analysis','React Native feasibility review (Engineering)','EU mobile OS market share data','iOS app performance metrics 60-day report'],
 'Build Android app using React Native, targeting Google Play launch by July 2. Prioritize feature parity with iOS app at launch.',
 'React Native enables an 8-week Android build by sharing the iOS checkout and account management components. Android is critical for EU expansion where Android market share is 68% (vs 32% iOS). Delay further risks our European growth momentum.',
 'Android app Google Play rating ≥4.4/5 within 60 days; Android subscriber conversion rate improvement ≥15% vs. mobile web; EU-market Android subscribers ≥200 in first 60 days.',
 '2026-07-02',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-04-02 10:00:00+00'),

(18,
 'Launch social sharing feature with referral reward ($15 credit)',
 'product',
 'Word-of-mouth accounts for 22% of new subscriber acquisitions in exit surveys of sign-up origin. We have no structured referral program. Hypothesis: a built-in share + $15 credit reward for the referrer (when the referred subscriber activates their first box) will amplify organic WOM into a measurable acquisition channel.',
 '[{"option":"No referral program","pros":["no cost per acquisition via referral"],"cons":["leave organic WOM unmonetized","WOM already at 22% without incentive — incentive would amplify"]},{"option":"$15 credit for referrer on first activated referral","pros":["aligned incentive — referrer only paid for real activations","$15 credit < $41 CAC so economics positive"],"cons":["requires fraud prevention","credit accounting complexity"]},{"option":"$15 cash discount for both referrer and referee","pros":["stronger two-sided incentive"],"cons":["$30 total cost per acquisition","higher fraud surface"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Acquisition source survey analysis 2025','Referral program benchmarks (Dropbox, Airbnb, Harry''s)','Fraud risk assessment: referral program','CAC analysis by channel Q4 2025'],
 'Launch one-sided referral program: $15 account credit for the referrer when a referred subscriber completes their first box. Include social share buttons in post-ship email and app.',
 'One-sided referral (referrer only) has lower fraud surface and is simpler to communicate. $15 credit is 37% of CAC ($41), making economics strongly positive. Post-ship email is the highest-intent moment to prompt sharing — subscribers have just received their box.',
 'Referral program generates ≥150 new subscribers per month by month 3; referral CAC ≤$20; referral-acquired subscriber 90-day retention ≥75%.',
 '2026-08-16',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-04-16 14:00:00+00'),

(19,
 'Integrate third-party gift card marketplace (GiftCards.com, Raise)',
 'product',
 'Gift subscriptions are 22% of Q4 revenue but require the buyer to know what they want in advance. Gift cards on secondary marketplaces (GiftCards.com, Raise) reach buyers who want flexibility. Integration cost is low; revenue impact is incremental since these are new distribution points with no direct cannibalization.',
 '[{"option":"No gift card marketplace","pros":["simple"],"cons":["miss distribution channel","gift card buyers are impulse buyers who need discovery"]},{"option":"Integrate GiftCards.com and Raise via API","pros":["incremental distribution","gift card buyers are net-new audience","low integration cost"],"cons":["marketplace takes 5-8% commission"]},{"option":"Build own gift card system on website only","pros":["100% margin"],"cons":["no new audience reach — same traffic we already have"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Gift card marketplace traffic analysis (GiftCards.com)','Raise integration API documentation','Commission structure: gift card marketplace comparison','Subscription gift card success cases (Birchbox, FabFitFun)'],
 'Integrate Nexura gift cards on GiftCards.com and Raise. Accept 7% marketplace commission on gift card sales. Launch in time for Q3 gifting season.',
 'Gift card marketplaces reach a different buyer profile than our organic traffic — they are impulse buyers looking for gift ideas. The 7% commission is acceptable for a fully incremental revenue stream with no marketing spend.',
 'Gift card marketplace sales ≥100 units/month by month 3; redemption rate ≥65% (indicating real gift buyers vs arbitrage); no cannibalization of direct gift subscription sales.',
 '2026-09-07',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-05-07 09:00:00+00'),

(20,
 'Build in-app skincare routine builder tool',
 'product',
 'Subscriber churn analysis shows the top driver of voluntary cancellation is "not sure how to use all the products." A guided skincare routine builder — showing subscribers which products to use in which order, morning vs night — addresses this directly. It is also a sticky feature that increases app session frequency.',
 '[{"option":"Static how-to content (blog posts)","pros":["fast","low cost"],"cons":["not personalized","low engagement with static content"]},{"option":"Interactive in-app routine builder","pros":["personalized to their specific box contents","increases app engagement","directly addresses churn driver"],"cons":["4-week build time","requires product data layer"]},{"option":"Video tutorials by product category","pros":["high engagement potential"],"cons":["production cost high","not personalized to box"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Churn exit survey: reason analysis 2025','App engagement session analysis (Mixpanel)','Product usage tutorial content engagement report','Engineering capacity Q2 2026'],
 'Build personalized routine builder in the app. On box delivery, the app generates a morning/night routine card using only the products in the subscriber''s current box. Build time: 3.5 weeks.',
 'If 31% of voluntary churn is product-confusion-driven and we convert even 30% of those to retained subscribers through routine education, the retention value far exceeds build cost. The routine builder is also a strong push notification hook ("Your morning routine is ready").',
 'Routine builder engagement ≥35% of subscribers within 30 days; voluntary churn rate decrease ≥0.4pp; app session frequency +20% for routine builder users.',
 '2026-09-22',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-05-22 11:00:00+00'),

(21,
 'Launch subscriber community forum (MVP)',
 'product',
 'Subscriber-created Facebook groups have organically formed without any product from us (largest has 14,000 members). Community is a proven retention lever in subscription commerce — Peloton, FabFitFun, and ipsy all cite community as a top-3 retention driver. An owned community is also a zero-cost acquisition surface.',
 '[{"option":"Leave community on Facebook","pros":["zero cost","already self-sustaining"],"cons":["no data ownership","Facebook algorithm risk","cannot integrate with product"]},{"option":"Build owned forum on Nexura platform","pros":["data ownership","deep product integration (share your box, rate products)","can moderate and control experience"],"cons":["8-week build","cold start — must migrate existing Facebook members"]},{"option":"Use Discourse as white-label forum","pros":["faster — 2-week setup","proven forum software"],"cons":["less integrated with product","Discourse branding visible"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Facebook group analysis: member count, engagement rate','Competitor community analysis (Peloton, FabFitFun)','Discourse vs custom build feasibility review','Retention correlation study: community-engaged vs non-engaged subscribers'],
 'Build owned community forum MVP in 8 weeks. Features: box reveal sharing, product rating, ask-the-expert Q&A, monthly theme threads. Seed with migration campaign to Facebook group members.',
 'Owning the community data and experience is strategically critical. Facebook groups are a liability — algorithm changes or platform policy changes could destroy the community overnight. Building now while organic momentum is strong is the right timing.',
 'Community forum MAU ≥3,000 within 90 days of launch; Facebook group migration conversion ≥30%; community-engaged subscriber retention rate ≥10pp above non-engaged baseline.',
 '2026-10-05',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Product',
 'Lena Fischer',
 '2026-06-05 09:00:00+00'),

(22,
 'Add product review and rating system to subscriber account',
 'product',
 'We collect no structured product feedback post-delivery. Curation decisions rely on supplier data and category buyer judgment. A subscriber-facing rating system generates proprietary preference data to improve curation, feeds the recommendation engine (decision 13), and surfaces social proof for the marketing team.',
 '[{"option":"Continue without ratings","pros":["no engineering cost"],"cons":["curation decisions remain judgment-based","recommendation engine lacks quality signal","no social proof for marketing"]},{"option":"5-star rating + optional text review per product","pros":["rich quality signal","social proof","feeds recommendation engine"],"cons":["4-week build","requires moderation workflow for text reviews"]},{"option":"Thumbs up/down only (simpler)","pros":["faster to build — 1 week"],"cons":["less granular signal for recommendations"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Recommendation engine data requirements (ML team)','Competitor review system analysis','Moderation workflow estimate (Trust & Safety)','Product quality complaints in CS tickets 2025'],
 'Build 5-star product rating system with optional text review. Triggered in-app 7 days after box delivery. Text reviews moderated by CS team before publishing.',
 '5-star ratings provide the quality signal the recommendation engine needs. Text reviews, while requiring moderation, provide qualitative curation intelligence that complements rating data. The 7-day post-delivery trigger catches subscribers at peak product engagement.',
 'Rating submission rate ≥40% of box deliveries; average data coverage ≥8 ratings per product per month; recommendation engine click-through rate +5pp above baseline after quality signal integration.',
 '2026-10-18',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Product',
 'Priya Menon',
 '2026-06-18 14:00:00+00');


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- HIRING (10 decisions)
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

INSERT INTO decisions (id, title, category, context, options_considered, data_consulted,
  decision_made, rationale, expected_outcome, review_date, status, actual_outcome, team, owner, decided_at)
VALUES
(23,
 'Hire Head of Data Science to build internal ML capability',
 'hiring',
 'We are outsourcing all ML/analytics work to a consultancy at $22K/month. Roadmap items (recommendation engine, churn prediction, demand forecasting) require sustained ML investment that consultancies cannot efficiently provide. A Head of Data Science can hire and lead a small team, own the data infrastructure, and ship models in-house.',
 '[{"option":"Continue with ML consultancy","pros":["flexible, no headcount","immediate capacity"],"cons":["$264K/year with no IP ownership","slow iteration cycles","no institutional knowledge"]},{"option":"Hire Head of Data Science (FTE, $180K total comp)","pros":["builds permanent capability","IP ownership","can hire junior team","faster iteration"],"cons":["6-8 week hiring timeline","onboarding lag"]},{"option":"Hire mid-level ML engineer instead","pros":["lower cost","faster hire"],"cons":["lacks strategic vision to build a team and data platform"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['ML consultancy invoice analysis 2025 ($264K/year)','Internal ML roadmap requirements','Head of Data Science salary benchmarks (Levels.fyi)','Make vs buy analysis: ML capability'],
 'Hire a Head of Data Science. Target: $180K total comp, 8-week timeline. Requirements: 5+ years industry ML, experience hiring and managing a team, Python/SQL proficient. Terminate consultancy engagement on new hire''s first day.',
 'The ML roadmap — recommendation engine, churn predictor, demand forecasting — requires sustained, fast-iteration capability that consultancies structurally cannot provide. At $180K vs $264K consultancy, the hire pays for itself immediately and builds permanent institutional knowledge.',
 'Head of Data Science hired and onboarded by March 1; consultancy terminated on hire start date; first ML model shipped within 45 days of onboarding.',
 '2026-04-06',
 'succeeded',
 'Priya Menon hired, start date Feb 15. Consultancy terminated Feb 14 (saving $22K/month from day 1). Recommendation engine shipped March 8 — 21 days after onboarding. Churn prediction model delivered April 2 with 82% precision. Priya is already interviewing for 2 ML engineer direct reports.',
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-01-06 10:00:00+00'),

(24,
 'Expand Customer Success team from 8 to 13 agents',
 'hiring',
 'CS team handles 3,200 tickets/week with average response time of 18 hours. Industry benchmark for subscription e-commerce is 4 hours. CSAT score is 3.8/5. Poor CS response time appears in exit surveys as the #3 churn driver. Current team of 8 is at capacity with projected subscriber growth in Q1.',
 '[{"option":"Hold at 8 agents — improve tooling instead","pros":["no headcount cost","automation may solve it"],"cons":["18-hour response time is a real churn driver — tooling alone will not close the gap fast enough"]},{"option":"Hire 5 agents (to 13 total)","pros":["closes response time gap","covers projected Q1 volume growth","one new team lead can be promoted internally"],"cons":["$280K annualized headcount cost"]},{"option":"Hire 3 agents and add chatbot","pros":["smaller headcount investment"],"cons":["chatbot implementation takes 8 weeks — no short-term relief"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['CS ticket volume and response time analysis Dec 2025','CSAT survey 2025 (score: 3.8)','Exit survey: CS as churn driver analysis','Headcount cost model: CS agents','Response time benchmark: subscription e-commerce (Zendesk 2025 report)'],
 'Hire 5 additional CS agents. Target: all 5 hired and fully trained by February 28. Internal promotion of senior agent Emma Park to Team Lead.',
 'At 18-hour response time we are 4.5× above the 4-hour industry benchmark. This is a measurable churn driver that cannot be solved by tooling alone in the near term. Adding 5 agents closes the volume gap and enables the team lead to introduce quality programs that improve CSAT.',
 'Average response time ≤4 hours within 60 days of full team ramp; CSAT score ≥4.3/5; CS-related churn mention in exit surveys falls by ≥30%.',
 '2026-03-20',
 'succeeded',
 'All 5 agents hired and trained by Feb 26. Emma Park promoted to Team Lead Mar 1. Average response time: 3.8 hours by March 20 (vs 18-hour baseline). CSAT: 4.5/5. CS-related churn mentions in exit surveys fell 48% (from 19% to 10% of cancel reasons).',
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-01-20 09:00:00+00'),

(25,
 'Hire 2 Senior Backend Engineers to reduce API latency and payment reliability',
 'hiring',
 'API p95 latency is 840ms — 2.4× our 350ms target. Payment service has had 2 outages in Q4 2025 totaling 4.2 hours of downtime. Engineering team has 4 backend engineers but product delivery has consumed all capacity. We need dedicated infrastructure and reliability engineers.',
 '[{"option":"Reassign existing engineers to infra work","pros":["no hiring cost","immediate"],"cons":["stops product delivery entirely","not a permanent solution"]},{"option":"Hire 2 Senior Backend Engineers ($175K each)","pros":["permanent capacity addition","infrastructure-focused from day 1","unblocks product team to continue delivery"],"cons":["8-week hiring timeline","$350K headcount cost"]},{"option":"Hire 1 engineer + contract SRE","pros":["faster and cheaper short-term"],"cons":["SRE contractor cost $200/hr — expensive for sustained work"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['API performance report Q4 2025','Payment service outage postmortems (2 incidents)','Engineering team capacity plan Q1 2026','Senior Backend Engineer salary benchmarks'],
 'Hire 2 Senior Backend Engineers with infrastructure focus. Target March 1 start date. Roles: (1) API performance and observability, (2) payment service reliability.',
 'API latency and payment reliability are blocking subscriber growth — slow pages hurt conversion and payment failures directly cost revenue. Two focused senior engineers will solve problems that the product-oriented team cannot prioritize without stopping feature delivery.',
 'API p95 latency ≤350ms; payment service uptime ≥99.95%; zero revenue-impacting outages in 90 days post-hire.',
 '2026-04-04',
 'succeeded',
 'Both engineers started March 1. API p95 latency reduced from 840ms to 380ms by April 1, and to 290ms by April 4. Payment service uptime: 99.97% (zero outages). Engineers shipped distributed tracing (OpenTelemetry) and payment retry logic in their first 4 weeks.',
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-02-04 11:00:00+00'),

(26,
 'Hire Vice President of Marketing',
 'hiring',
 'We have been operating with a marketing director and no VP-level marketing leader for 9 months. Brand, performance, and content functions are siloed. Product-led growth is our primary motion but we need senior marketing leadership to scale paid acquisition, manage agency relationships, and build the brand for EU expansion.',
 '[{"option":"Promote Marketing Director Raj internally","pros":["institutional knowledge","fast","no recruiting cost"],"cons":["Raj lacks paid acquisition experience at scale","promotion may not be right for the scope"]},{"option":"External VP hire ($210K total comp)","pros":["brings EU-market experience and agency relationships","senior enough to own the full function"],"cons":["6-10 week search","cultural fit risk"]},{"option":"Fractional CMO + hire later","pros":["faster","lower cost","buy time"],"cons":["fractional CMO cannot own execution","creates confusion on accountability"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Marketing function audit Jan 2026','VP Marketing salary benchmarks (Levels.fyi)','EU expansion marketing requirements analysis','Internal: Raj''s performance review and growth feedback'],
 'Hire external VP of Marketing with EU-market experience. Budget: $210K total comp. Target start: March 1. Requirements: subscription commerce background, managed $2M+ paid acquisition budget, EU market expansion experience.',
 'The EU expansion (decisions 33-40) requires a senior marketing leader who has done this before. Internal promotion of Raj risks setting him up to fail on a scope that exceeds his current experience. An external hire brings the specific EU-market pattern-matching we need.',
 'VP hired and onboarded by March 1; EU marketing strategy documented by April 15; paid acquisition CAC held at ≤$45 during onboarding period.',
 '2026-05-16',
 'failed',
 'Alex Torres hired, start date March 1. Persistent strategic misalignment with our product-led growth model — Alex advocated for brand-first campaigns while our model is built on self-serve trial conversion. Performance improvement plan issued at day 45. Alex resigned on day 58. Total recruiting cost: $90K. EU marketing strategy not delivered. Search restarted with clearer PLG-aligned brief. Key lesson: VP Marketing spec must explicitly state product-led growth model as a non-negotiable context.',
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-02-16 14:00:00+00'),

(27,
 'Hire 3 Machine Learning Engineers to scale the data science team',
 'hiring',
 'Head of Data Science Priya Menon (hired February 15) has delivered the recommendation engine and begun the churn model but is personally bandwidth-constrained. Roadmap includes demand forecasting, pricing optimization, and EU personalization localization — all requiring engineering execution. Priya has recommended hiring 3 ML engineers.',
 '[{"option":"Hire 1 ML engineer now, more later","pros":["lower burn rate","validate team model first"],"cons":["churn predictor and demand forecasting will slip 6+ months","data science bottleneck limits product roadmap"]},{"option":"Hire 3 ML engineers (Priya''s recommendation)","pros":["fully staffed to execute 2026 ML roadmap","Priya can shift to strategic architecture","each engineer owns one model domain"],"cons":["$420K headcount cost","3 simultaneous searches are operationally demanding"]},{"option":"Expand consultancy instead of FTEs","pros":["flexible"],"cons":["already proven consultancy is slow and expensive — see decision 23"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['ML roadmap requirements 2026 (Priya Menon)','ML engineer salary benchmarks (Levels.fyi)','Data science team structure benchmarks (similar-stage companies)','Product roadmap: ML-dependent features list'],
 'Hire 3 ML Engineers at $155K total comp each. Roles: (1) Churn and LTV modeling, (2) Demand forecasting and inventory, (3) Personalization and recommendation systems. Target April 1 start date.',
 'Priya has proven she can ship models fast but cannot do it alone at the roadmap pace required. Each engineer domain-owning a specific model area is the proven team structure for ML product organizations. The consultancy path has already been proven not to work (see decision 23).',
 'All 3 engineers hired by April 1; churn prediction model in production by May 15; demand forecasting model reducing stockout rate by ≥30% by June 1.',
 '2026-06-06',
 'succeeded',
 'All 3 ML engineers started April 1. Churn prediction model in production May 2 with 82% precision (ROC-AUC 0.89). Demand forecasting model reduced stockout rate from 8.1% to 2.3% (71% reduction — above 30% target). Personalization engineer shipped A/B test framework for localized EU recommendations.',
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-03-06 09:00:00+00'),

(28,
 'Outsource QA testing function to offshore partner',
 'hiring',
 'QA testing is conducted by 2 internal QA engineers at $130K each. Offshore partner Testify Pro offers equivalent coverage for $4,200/month (3-person team). Projected annual saving: $215K. Leadership has pressure to reduce burn rate while maintaining pace.',
 '[{"option":"Keep internal QA team","pros":["deep product knowledge","fast feedback loops","culture fit"],"cons":["$260K/year cost","slower iteration on offshore alternative"]},{"option":"Outsource to Testify Pro ($4,200/month)","pros":["$215K/year savings","flexible capacity scaling"],"cons":["ramp-up time","potential quality gap","timezone lag"]},{"option":"Hybrid: keep 1 internal QA lead, outsource 2 roles","pros":["quality oversight retained","partial savings"],"cons":["complex management overhead","only partial cost savings"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['QA cost analysis 2025','Testify Pro proposal and references','QA defect escape rate benchmarks','Internal QA team performance review 2025 (defect escape rate: 0.8%)'],
 'Transition to Testify Pro for full QA coverage. Internal QA engineers given 30-day notice. Transition period: 4 weeks of overlap and knowledge transfer.',
 'The cost savings are real and the Testify Pro reference checks were positive. A 4-week transition with internal team overlap should provide adequate knowledge transfer. The 0.8% defect escape rate sets a clear quality benchmark to hold the vendor to.',
 'Defect escape rate ≤1.2% at 60 days (20% buffer above internal baseline); no P0 bugs in production in first 60 days; monthly cost ≤$4,500.',
 '2026-05-22',
 'reversed',
 'Transition completed April 1. Defect escape rate in first 30 days: 4.1% — 5× the internal baseline and 3.4× the contracted SLA. A P1 payment processing bug reached production on April 18 causing $12K in failed transactions. Decision reversed on April 20; Testify Pro contract terminated. Internal QA team (both engineers) were retained — neither had accepted other offers. Total cost: transition friction + payment bug remediation. Key lesson: QA is a core function that requires product context; offshore transition requires 90-day parallel run, not 30 days.',
 'Engineering',
 'Paulo Rivera',
 '2026-03-22 10:00:00+00'),

(29,
 'Hire 2 Product Managers for core product and growth tracks',
 'hiring',
 'Product team has 1 PM (Lena Fischer) managing a 12-person engineering+design org. PM capacity is the primary bottleneck on product delivery — discovery, specs, and stakeholder alignment take Lena''s full time, leaving no capacity for strategic roadmap development or new initiative incubation.',
 '[{"option":"Hold at 1 PM — Lena manages everything","pros":["no cost"],"cons":["bottleneck is real — roadmap delivery is slipping","Lena is at risk of burnout"]},{"option":"Hire 2 PMs: Core Product PM and Growth PM","pros":["doubles PM capacity","clear domain ownership","Lena moves to VP of Product role"],"cons":["$280K headcount cost","6-8 week search"]},{"option":"Hire 1 senior PM to support Lena","pros":["lower cost","faster hire"],"cons":["does not fully relieve the bottleneck — still single point of failure"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Product delivery velocity report Q1 2026','PM capacity model vs. roadmap requirements','PM salary benchmarks (Levels.fyi)','Lena Fischer 1:1 feedback: burnout risk assessment'],
 'Hire 2 Product Managers: (1) Core Product PM focused on subscriber experience and retention features; (2) Growth PM focused on acquisition, referral, and monetization. Target start date: June 15. Promote Lena Fischer to VP of Product.',
 'A single PM managing a 12-person team is unsustainable at our current growth pace. The Growth PM track is particularly high-value given the EU expansion and new monetization initiatives in the roadmap. Promoting Lena to VP creates the management structure needed for scale.',
 'Both PMs hired by June 15; product delivery cycle time reduced ≥20% by Q3; Lena''s reported workload stress score improves from 7.8 to ≤5.0/10.',
 '2026-08-10',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-04-10 14:00:00+00'),

(30,
 'Hire Director of International Expansion',
 'hiring',
 'EU expansion is active in UK and Canada (decisions 33, 34) and planned for France, Spain, Netherlands, and Nordics (decisions 37-40). All EU operations are currently managed by the CEO on top of existing responsibilities. A dedicated Director of International Expansion is needed to own market entry execution, local partnerships, and regulatory compliance.',
 '[{"option":"CEO continues managing EU expansion","pros":["no cost","direct founder-led relationships in new markets"],"cons":["unsustainable — EU complexity will only grow","diverts CEO from strategic priorities"]},{"option":"Hire Director of International Expansion ($160K total comp)","pros":["dedicated ownership","brings EU-market operational experience","CEO returns to US strategy focus"],"cons":["6-8 week search","requires strong EU market network"]},{"option":"Promote UK Country Manager to regional role","pros":["market knowledge","no search time"],"cons":["current UK manager lacks multi-country experience"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['CEO time audit: EU expansion time spend (40% of hours)','EU expansion roadmap 2026 (France, Spain, Netherlands, Nordics)','Director of Intl Expansion salary benchmarks','UK Country Manager performance and growth assessment'],
 'Hire a Director of International Expansion with European subscription commerce experience. Budget: $160K total comp. Target start: July 1. Reports to CEO.',
 'At 4 active and 4 planned EU market entries, EU operations have passed the complexity threshold where a dedicated operational leader is required. The CEO spending 40% of time on EU execution is not sustainable for either the CEO or the quality of EU market operations.',
 'Director hired and onboarded by July 1; France and Spain market entry milestones on track by Q3; CEO EU time freed ≥25% of current 40%.',
 '2026-08-24',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-04-24 09:00:00+00'),

(31,
 'Hire 4 EU-based Customer Success representatives',
 'hiring',
 'UK and Canada subscribers are currently supported by the US CS team operating 9am-6pm ET. UK subscribers experience up to 14-hour response delays due to timezone gap. France and Spain launches (Q3 2026) will add non-English speakers who cannot be served by the current team. EU-local CS agents are required.',
 '[{"option":"Continue US CS for all markets","pros":["no cost","single team"],"cons":["14-hour timezone gap for UK","language barrier for France/Spain","below-4-hour SLA cannot be maintained"]},{"option":"Hire 4 EU agents (2 UK, 1 France, 1 Spain)","pros":["timezone coverage for all EU markets","native language support","sets foundation for EU CS org"],"cons":["$260K headcount cost","remote management complexity"]},{"option":"Outsource EU CS to BPO (after QA outsourcing failure in decision 28)","pros":["faster, lower cost"],"cons":["BPO quality risk is demonstrated — see decision 28"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['UK subscriber response time analysis','CS ticket language breakdown post-Canada launch','France and Spain market launch plan (timelines)','EU CS salary benchmarks (London, Paris, Madrid)'],
 'Hire 4 EU CS representatives: 2 in London (UK/English), 1 in Paris (France/French), 1 in Madrid (Spain/Spanish). All report to CS Team Lead Emma Park. Target start: August 1.',
 'Timezone-appropriate, language-native CS is a non-negotiable for scaling in EU. The BPO option is off the table given the QA outsourcing failure (decision 28). An internal EU team builds institutional product knowledge and maintains the quality standards we have established.',
 'EU subscriber response time ≤4 hours; EU CSAT ≥4.2/5; EU CS-related churn mentions ≤10% of EU cancel reasons.',
 '2026-09-12',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-05-12 10:00:00+00'),

(32,
 'Hire Chief Financial Officer to replace departing CFO',
 'hiring',
 'CFO Maria Santos has announced her departure for a Series C opportunity. We are pre-Series B with EU expansion creating significant financial complexity: multi-currency reporting, VAT compliance across 6 EU jurisdictions, EU transfer pricing, and an upcoming fundraise. The CFO role is critical to fill before Maria''s July 31 departure.',
 '[{"option":"Promote VP Finance Amara Diallo to CFO","pros":["deep institutional knowledge","fast transition","zero search cost"],"cons":["Amara lacks public-company and fundraising experience","Series B preparation requires specific skills"]},{"option":"External CFO hire ($240K total comp)","pros":["fundraising and EU financial expertise","Series B readiness","independent perspective on strategy"],"cons":["8-10 week search — tight vs July 31 departure","transition risk"]},{"option":"Interim fractional CFO while we search","pros":["buys time for right hire","lower cost during search"],"cons":["investors prefer FTE CFO in fundraising process"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Maria Santos departure timeline and transition plan','Series B fundraising preparation requirements','EU VAT compliance complexity assessment','CFO salary benchmarks: pre-Series B SaaS/ecomm'],
 'Run external CFO search immediately. Target July 15 offer acceptance to allow 2-week overlap with Maria before July 31. Use executive search firm Korn Ferry. Amara Diallo to serve as Acting CFO if gap exists.',
 'The Series B fundraise target (Q4 2026) and EU financial complexity require a CFO with direct experience in both. Promoting Amara risks her success on a larger scope than she has operated in. Korn Ferry can compress the search to 8 weeks with our target profile.',
 'CFO hired with start date ≤Aug 15; Series B prep materials initiated within 30 days of hire; VAT compliance framework across all EU markets by Q3.',
 '2026-10-10',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'People',
 'James Okafor',
 '2026-06-10 14:00:00+00');


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- MARKET_ENTRY (8 decisions)
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

INSERT INTO decisions (id, title, category, context, options_considered, data_consulted,
  decision_made, rationale, expected_outcome, review_date, status, actual_outcome, team, owner, decided_at)
VALUES
(33,
 'Launch Nexura in the United Kingdom market',
 'market_entry',
 'UK is the largest English-speaking subscription box market outside North America, with £1.2B in annual subscription box revenue. UK consumers have demonstrated strong adoption of US wellness brands. We have identified a UK 3PL partner (Clipper Logistics) and UK-based content creator partnerships. Regulatory: UK-REACH cosmetics compliance is achievable within 60 days.',
 '[{"option":"Delay UK — focus on US growth","pros":["operational simplicity"],"cons":["UK market window closing as competitors move","first-mover advantage diminishing"]},{"option":"UK launch via Clipper Logistics 3PL","pros":["fastest to market","proven UK 3PL","no fixed cost infrastructure"],"cons":["3PL margin hit of £2.80/box","dependency on single partner"]},{"option":"UK warehouse owned by Nexura","pros":["full control","lower per-unit cost at scale"],"cons":["18-month setup","£400K capex — premature at this stage"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['UK subscription box market sizing (Mintel 2025)','Clipper Logistics UK pricing proposal','UK-REACH cosmetics compliance assessment','UK consumer survey: beauty subscription interest (n=800)','Currency risk analysis: GBP/USD'],
 'Launch UK market via Clipper Logistics 3PL. Target first UK deliveries by February 15. Initial marketing: 5 UK creator partnerships and £30K paid acquisition budget.',
 'UK is the clearest path for international expansion: English-language content works without translation, regulatory compliance is achievable, and US wellness brands have proven pull. Clipper Logistics handles customs clearance. 3PL model validates UK unit economics before any capex commitment.',
 '≥1,000 UK subscribers within 90 days; UK blended CAC ≤£35; UK subscriber LTV tracking at ≥£85 at 6-month proxy.',
 '2026-04-10',
 'succeeded',
 '1,240 UK subscribers at 90-day mark — 24% above forecast. Blended UK CAC: £31 (11% below target). UK LTV 6-month proxy: £91. UK CSAT: 4.4/5. Clipper Logistics on-time delivery: 97%. UK creator partnership CPAs ranged £19-£38; 3 of 5 are being renewed.',
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-01-10 10:00:00+00'),

(34,
 'Expand into Canada: English-speaking provinces first',
 'pricing',
 'Canada is geographically adjacent, English-speaking (in target provinces), and has demonstrated strong US wellness brand adoption. Canadian duty on our product category is 6.5%, manageable. We can fulfill from our US fulfillment center in Ohio with no new 3PL partnership required, using DHL Express Canada.',
 '[{"option":"Skip Canada — focus on Europe","pros":["concentrated resource on EU expansion"],"cons":["Canada is lowest-friction international expansion possible — wrong to skip"]},{"option":"Canada via DHL from Ohio FC","pros":["no new infrastructure","operational in 3 weeks","familiar logistics partner"],"cons":["longer delivery times (3-5 days)","6.5% duty adds C$3.20/box"]},{"option":"Canadian 3PL partnership","pros":["faster delivery","lower per-box duty treatment"],"cons":["4-6 month setup","premature at validation stage"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Canada cross-border e-commerce feasibility study','DHL Express Canada pricing and delivery time analysis','Canadian duty rates: cosmetics and wellness category','Canadian subscriber survey: interest and WTP (n=400)'],
 'Launch Canada via DHL from Ohio FC. Target provinces: Ontario, British Columbia, Quebec (English-speakers). Launch by March 1. CAD pricing at C$65/month.',
 'The Ohio FC to Canada route is already tested by DHL. Canada represents a low-risk validation of international operations with minimal new infrastructure. If unit economics are positive, we invest in a Canadian 3PL by Q4 2026.',
 '≥500 Canadian subscribers in 90 days; blended CAC ≤C$45; unit economics positive (margin ≥35%) after duty and shipping.',
 '2026-05-06',
 'succeeded',
 '662 Canadian subscribers at 90-day mark — 32% above target. CAC: C$38 (16% below target). Unit margin: 38% after duty and DHL cost. Average delivery time: 3.8 days to Toronto, 4.2 days to Vancouver. Decision to pursue Canadian 3PL partnership in Q4 2026 already advancing.',
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-02-06 11:00:00+00'),

(35,
 'Launch in the Australian market targeting major metro areas',
 'market_entry',
 'Australia has a $380M subscription box market with limited local competition in premium wellness. English-speaking, high income per capita, and strong US brand affinity. Proposed model: ship from US via Australia Post partner, target Sydney and Melbourne first.',
 '[{"option":"Skip Australia","pros":["focus on EU where competition is weaker"],"cons":["Australia market opportunity is real"]},{"option":"Launch via US shipping + Australia Post","pros":["no new infrastructure","fastest to market"],"cons":["$28-34 AUD shipping cost per box — unclear unit economics","12-17 day delivery time"]},{"option":"Australian 3PL partnership before launch","pros":["sustainable unit economics","4-5 day delivery"],"cons":["6-month setup — delays entry"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Australia subscription box market sizing (IBIS World 2025)','US-to-Australia shipping quotes: FedEx, DHL, Australia Post','Duty and customs: Australian cosmetics import rules','Unit economics model: Australian market'],
 'Launch Australia via US-origin shipping using DHL Express Australia. Test with $50K paid acquisition budget over 60 days. Evaluate unit economics before committing further.',
 'The market opportunity is real and English-speaking markets are our highest-success profile. DHL pricing was quoted at $18 USD per box — we modeled this as acceptable at AUD$89 selling price. 60-day test limits exposure while validating demand and logistics.',
 '≥300 Australian subscribers in 60 days; unit economics positive at AUD$89 price point; delivery time ≤10 days.',
 '2026-05-22',
 'failed',
 'After 60 days: 142 subscribers (53% of target). Landed unit cost was AUD$31 per box (vs AUD$18 model — DHL surcharge and customs inspection added $13) making the business model structurally negative at AUD$89. Market exit decision made May 2. $50K acquisition budget was paused early. Key learning: always get firm DHL AU quotes with customs inspection risk factored in — published rates exclude inspection delays which are common for cosmetics at Australian customs.',
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-02-22 14:00:00+00'),

(36,
 'Germany market entry via B2B wellness corporate gifting partnerships',
 'market_entry',
 'Germany is the largest EU economy and a strong wellness market. Initial hypothesis: instead of DTC (which requires German-language content and GDPR full compliance), enter via B2B corporate gifting partnerships with HR/wellbeing platforms that already have German corporate clients.',
 '[{"option":"Germany DTC launch","pros":["full market access","highest LTV subscribers"],"cons":["German-language content required","GDPR compliance complex","high CAC in new market"]},{"option":"Germany via B2B corporate gifting (HR platforms)","pros":["English-language relationship possible","low regulatory complexity","HR platform handles GDPR","faster to revenue"],"cons":["B2B margin lower","limited scale ceiling"]},{"option":"Skip Germany — France first","pros":["France DTC model already planned"],"cons":["miss largest EU market opportunity"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Germany wellness market sizing (Roland Berger 2025)','B2B corporate gifting platform landscape (Germany)','GDPR compliance cost estimate for German DTC','German HR platform partnership outreach results'],
 'Pursue Germany B2B entry via partnership with 2-3 HR wellbeing platforms. Target: first corporate client by April 30.',
 'B2B corporate gifting reduces the language and regulatory barrier for Germany entry while we build German-language content and GDPR-compliant infrastructure for a future DTC launch. The HR platform partnerships create a bridgehead that can generate revenue immediately.',
 'First German corporate gifting contract signed by April 30; ≥500 B2B gift units delivered in Q2; margin ≥25% on B2B channel.',
 '2026-06-12',
 'superseded',
 'B2B model de-prioritized after DTC analysis in April showed 3.2× higher LTV for German DTC subscribers vs B2B corporate gift recipients. Two HR platform conversations were advanced but paused. New Germany DTC-first strategy approved May 2026 (see decision 37 for France as the DTC template). Germany DTC launch now planned for Q1 2027.',
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-03-12 09:00:00+00'),

(37,
 'France DTC launch: first non-English market entry',
 'market_entry',
 'France is Europe''s second-largest beauty and wellness market (€4.2B). French consumers are the most receptive to premium skincare among EU markets. France is our first non-English market, requiring full French-language content, EU-REACH compliance (already done for UK), and French CS coverage (decision 31). We will use the UK Clipper Logistics partnership as a model.',
 '[{"option":"Delay France until Germany proven","pros":["sequential market learning"],"cons":["France beauty market has strong pull — early entry advantage is real"]},{"option":"France DTC via French 3PL (Relais Colis)","pros":["same model as UK","French-native fulfillment","2-3 day delivery"],"cons":["French content translation cost (€8K)","French CS hire required (decision 31)"]},{"option":"France via Amazon.fr marketplace first","pros":["fast","French audience reach"],"cons":["Amazon erodes brand","no subscriber data ownership"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['France beauty and wellness market sizing (Euromonitor 2025)','Relais Colis partnership proposal','French consumer survey: premium subscription box interest (n=600)','EU-REACH compliance status (already complete)','French content localization cost estimate'],
 'Launch France DTC via Relais Colis 3PL. French-language website and email. French CS hire from decision 31. Target first French deliveries August 15. Marketing: 3 French creator partnerships + €25K paid acquisition.',
 'France is a natural second EU market after UK. The 3PL model is proven. French cosmetics culture aligns strongly with our product positioning. French content translation (€8K) is a trivial cost against the market opportunity. The French CS hire in decision 31 is already in progress.',
 '≥600 French subscribers in 90 days; French CAC ≤€40; CSAT ≥4.0/5 (adjusted for higher French service expectations).',
 '2026-08-05',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-04-05 10:00:00+00'),

(38,
 'Spain market entry: launch 90 days after France',
 'market_entry',
 'Spain is the 5th-largest EU economy with a growing wellness subscription market (+28% YoY). Spanish market entry can leverage the French operational model with Spanish-language localization. By launching 90 days after France, we apply learning from the France launch to Spain without delay.',
 '[{"option":"Spain immediately alongside France","pros":["no additional delay"],"cons":["operational risk of two new markets simultaneously"]},{"option":"Spain 90 days after France launch","pros":["apply France learning","staggered operational load","Spanish CS hire lined up (decision 31)"],"cons":["90-day delay vs simultaneous"]},{"option":"Skip Spain — consolidate in UK/France/Germany","pros":["operational focus"],"cons":["Spain market growing fast — opportunity cost of delay is high"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Spain subscription market sizing (Statista 2025)','Spanish consumer survey: wellness subscription interest','Spain 3PL options: MRW, Correos Express','Spain entry cost model: translation + 3PL + CS'],
 'Launch Spain 90 days after France (target November 15). Use MRW as Spanish 3PL. Spanish CS hire from decision 31. Spanish-language website and email.',
 'Sequential market entry (France then Spain) allows operational learning transfer. The Spanish market shows the same demand signals as France. MRW is the standard Spanish subscription commerce 3PL and has been pre-qualified.',
 '≥400 Spanish subscribers in 90 days; Spanish CAC ≤€42; operational COGS per box comparable to France (±10%).',
 '2026-08-20',
