(39,
 'Netherlands market entry: English-friendly low-friction test',
 'market_entry',
 'The Netherlands has the highest English proficiency in the EU (EF EPI #1 globally). This means Dutch market entry can be done with English-language content — no translation required. It is the lowest-cost EU market test with a premium-oriented consumer base and a population of 17.9M. Dutch 3PL PostNL is already handling UK overflow.',
 '[{"option":"Skip Netherlands — too small","pros":["focus on larger markets"],"cons":["English-language, high-income market requires zero localization cost — wrong to skip"]},{"option":"Netherlands with English content via PostNL","pros":["zero translation cost","PostNL relationship already exists","premium consumer base"],"cons":["smaller market than France/Spain","lower absolute subscriber ceiling"]},{"option":"Netherlands via German-language content (Flemish)","pros":["covers both Netherlands and Flanders Belgium"],"cons":["Dutch consumers prefer Dutch or English — German is wrong choice"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['EU English proficiency index (EF EPI 2025)','PostNL Netherlands pricing proposal','Netherlands subscription box market analysis','Dutch consumer sentiment: premium wellness brands'],
 'Launch Netherlands with English-language content via PostNL. No translation cost. Budget: €15K paid acquisition. Target September 14 first deliveries.',
 'No-translation, English-only EU market entry is a uniquely low-cost expansion. PostNL is already in our logistics network. The Netherlands validates whether our English-language brand can convert EU non-native markets — a data point useful for Germany and Nordics planning.',
 '≥250 Dutch subscribers in 90 days; CAC ≤€38; CSAT ≥4.1/5.',
 '2026-09-14',
 'active',
 NULL,
 'Growth',
 'Marco Delgado',
 '2026-05-14 09:00:00+00'),

(40,
 'Nordics regional launch covering Sweden, Denmark, and Norway',
 'market_entry',
 'The Nordics have the highest wellness spending per capita in Europe and near-universal English proficiency. Sweden, Denmark, and Norway can be served as a regional cluster with shared Scandinavian creator partnerships and PostNord as a regional 3PL. This is planned as a Q4 2026 launch, building on France and Spain operational learning.',
 '[{"option":"Nordics individually (Sweden first)","pros":["focused learning in single market"],"cons":["Nordics function as a regional consumer cluster — splitting them is suboptimal for creator partnerships and 3PL economics"]},{"option":"Nordics as a cluster (Sweden+Denmark+Norway simultaneously)","pros":["PostNord regional 3PL works across all 3","Scandinavian creators have cross-border reach","English-language content works in all 3"],"cons":["operational complexity of 3 new currencies (SEK, DKK, NOK)"]},{"option":"Nordics via Amazon (Amazon.se launched 2024)","pros":["fast","ready distribution"],"cons":["brand erosion","no subscriber data"]}]'::jsonb,
 ARRAY['Nordic wellness market sizing (Euromonitor 2025)','PostNord regional 3PL proposal','Nordic English proficiency data','Scandinavian influencer marketing landscape report','Currency: SEK/DKK/NOK management options (Stripe)'],
 'Launch Nordics as a regional cluster via PostNord. Three local currencies managed via Stripe. Scandinavian creator partnerships (5 influencers). Target first deliveries October 6.',
 'The Nordics are geographically and culturally contiguous — PostNord serves all three, the same creators have cross-border audiences, and English-language content works in all three markets. Managing 3 currencies via Stripe is operationally trivial. Cluster launch is more efficient than sequential single-country launches.',
 '≥350 combined Nordic subscribers (across SE/DK/NO) within 90 days; CAC ≤€45; PostNord on-time delivery ≥95%.',
